dnie-pkcs11-compat (0.2.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Release workflow: publish a riscv64 .deb assembled from the cross-compiled
    shim (packaging/debian/build-prebuilt.sh), so releases include packages for
    amd64, arm64 and riscv64.
  * Validation: Firefox client authentication (the site must advertise
    AC DNIE 004), T7–T9 on x86-64, aarch64 and riscv64, and PAdES plus C_Sign
    with the signing key on both boards.
  * Documentation: the DNIe user-consent prompt for signing
    (user_consent_enabled = false for unattended use), the pdfsig 26.08 false
    negative, the stale OpenSC cache after renewal, and the CA-list filter.

 -- ZiTAL <2283548+ZiTAL@users.noreply.github.com>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:30:00 +0100

dnie-pkcs11-compat (0.2.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * verify-card.sh clears the OpenSC card cache after certificate renewal.
  * test-tls-auth.sh: RFC 7512 CKA_ID encoding, no p11tool dependency, and
    no false-positive result when the client sends no certificate.
  * Documentation: ARM64 T10/T9 results, PIN metadata caveat, and the
    Firefox/Chromium client-certificate findings (Chromium needs TLS 1.2
    and RSA+SHA256; TLS 1.3 requires RSA-PSS).
  * Build scripts exclude local PIN/password and signing-test files.

